  "slug": "furfright",
  "name": "FurFright",
  "shortName": null,
  "description": "FurFright was a Halloween-themed anthropomorphic convention in Connecticut, founded in 2003 by Belic Bear and K'gra Leopard and held until 2013. It began as a one-day mini-convention at a cabin in Middletown, expecting 30 to 50 people, and more than 160 registered. It grew to a three-day convention, moving through the Sheraton Bradley Hotel in Windsor Locks, the Waterbury hotels and the Crowne Plaza in Cromwell, and in 2008 it was the fifth most attended furry convention in the world. An attendance cap of 1,500 was set in 2011. Typical events included a masquerade, a charity auction, a movie morgue, Fursuit Massacre games and trick-or-treating, and it supported animal and environmental charities, mainly the United States War Dog Association. After 2013 its staff started a successor convention, Furpocalypse.",
